course: dictionary
lesson: 8539
title: Woodwind or brass?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A saxophone is a musical instrument made of brass, shaped like a curved J. You play it by blowing into a mouthpiece with a reed and pressing keys to change the notes.
explain: «The saxophone is made of brass but is a woodwind, because it makes its sound with a reed, like a clarinet.» So brass tells you what the instrument is made of, but the family depends on how the sound is made.
explain: A reed is a thin strip of cane that vibrates when you blow on it. «The family of an instrument depends on how the sound is made.» The trumpet is brass because your lips must buzz.
fact: A saxophone is made of brass, but it belongs to the woodwind family.
fact: The sound of a saxophone is made by a reed, a thin vibrating strip of cane.
fact: Adolphe Sax invented the saxophone in Belgium in the 1840s.
fact: Saxophones come in soprano, alto, tenor and baritone sizes.
fact: The short form of saxophone is sax.
exercise: «The saxophone is made of brass but is a woodwind, because it makes its sound with a reed.» What family is the saxophone in? | Brass | *Woodwind | Percussion | Strings
exercise: What is the saxophone made of? | Plastic | Wood | *Brass | Cane
exercise: Which instrument is brass because your lips must buzz? | Saxophone | *Trumpet | Clarinet | Flute
test: What makes the sound in a saxophone? | Strings | *A reed | Lips buzzing | A drum skin
test: Which of these is a kind of saxophone? | Trombone | Harp | Cello | *Tenor
exam: Why is a shiny metal saxophone a woodwind? | *It uses a reed to make its sound | It is shaped like a flute | It is made of wood | It is played by hitting it
